1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
This is CueMend: a browser agent
repairs caption timing

2
00:00:04,162 --> 00:00:07,243
while a human protects
the performance.

3
00:00:07,243 --> 00:00:10,289
Here is the result first—zero conflicts

4
00:00:10,289 --> 00:00:12,997
and a verifiable,
editable export.

5
00:00:13,647 --> 00:00:17,223
We reset to a fictional
thirty-two-second rehearsal

6
00:00:17,223 --> 00:00:21,402
with ten captions and seven independent
timing problems.

7
00:00:21,402 --> 00:00:26,436
Automation can measure overlap,
reading rate, and visual collisions.

8
00:00:26,436 --> 00:00:29,579
It cannot decide whether
an audience laugh,

9
00:00:29,579 --> 00:00:33,399
lighting reveal, or actor's breath
deserves silence.

10
00:00:33,399 --> 00:00:36,718
Those decisions stay
in the human interface.

11
00:00:37,368 --> 00:00:40,437
Through Chrome's native Web M C P channel,

12
00:00:40,437 --> 00:00:45,265
the agent inspects the live revision,
audits the active track,

13
00:00:45,265 --> 00:00:47,860
and calls CueMend's staging tool.

14
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:51,084
The browser deterministically
evaluates all

15
00:00:51,084 --> 00:00:55,332
six thousand five hundred sixty-one
authored combinations,

16
00:00:55,332 --> 00:00:58,809
then exposes three
zero-conflict alternatives.

17
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:02,063
Staging never mutates
the active captions.

18
00:01:02,713 --> 00:01:05,693
The first live preview minimizes motion,

19
00:01:05,693 --> 00:01:08,924
but it crosses Jon's
optional final breath.

20
00:01:08,924 --> 00:01:13,463
The stage manager protects that beat
with one visible click.

21
00:01:13,463 --> 00:01:16,151
The workspace moves to revision two,

22
00:01:16,151 --> 00:01:21,414
the conflict count rises to eight,
and the old proposal becomes stale.

23
00:01:22,064 --> 00:01:25,554
When the agent retries
its revision-one request,

24
00:01:25,554 --> 00:01:29,443
CueMend returns stale revision
and changes nothing.

25
00:01:29,443 --> 00:01:33,988
The capability inventory also retires
unsafe proposal tools.

26
00:01:33,988 --> 00:01:36,969
The agent must inspect the current state

27
00:01:36,969 --> 00:01:40,200
and replan under
the new human constraint.

28
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:45,371
The new search finds
two hundred fifty-six legal tracks.

29
00:01:45,371 --> 00:01:47,650
The agent previews plan one,

30
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:51,381
but only the human can select
and approve it.

31
00:01:51,381 --> 00:01:55,391
Approval binds the exact proposal,
plan, revision,

32
00:01:55,391 --> 00:01:57,940
and S H A two fifty-six digest.

33
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:01,751
Only then does the one-shot
commit tool appear.

34
00:02:02,401 --> 00:02:06,204
The agent invokes that temporary
commit capability

35
00:02:06,204 --> 00:02:08,174
with an idempotency key.

36
00:02:08,174 --> 00:02:11,753
CueMend revalidates the approval
and beat locks

37
00:02:11,753 --> 00:02:13,800
before changing anything.

38
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:18,943
The shared page immediately shows
revision three, zero conflicts,

39
00:02:18,943 --> 00:02:22,325
a clean cue rail,
and an immutable receipt.

40
00:02:22,325 --> 00:02:24,372
Mutation tools disappear.

41
00:02:25,022 --> 00:02:29,314
Finally, the agent independently
re-audits the committed track

42
00:02:29,314 --> 00:02:33,772
and exports editable Web V T T
plus a limitations certificate.

43
00:02:33,772 --> 00:02:37,373
The certificate proves
this exact fictional fixture

44
00:02:37,373 --> 00:02:39,447
under the named demo profile;

45
00:02:39,447 --> 00:02:43,286
it does not claim universal
accessibility compliance.

46
00:02:43,286 --> 00:02:46,955
CueMend lets the agent do
exhaustive mechanical work

47
00:02:46,955 --> 00:02:49,267
while the human keeps the beat.
